"""One-off August 19 editorial revision: fresh facts and original decision points."""
from pathlib import Path
import json,runpy,sys
D='2025-08-19';sys.argv=[__file__,D]
R=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
e=runpy.run_path(str(R/'writer-middle/compose.py'));q=e['q'];obs=e['obs']
s=json.loads((R/'specs'/f'{D}.json').read_text())
def replace(block,rows):
 assert len(block['parts'])==len(rows)
 block['parts']=[[old[0],q(rx,topic,cat)+text] for old,(rx,topic,cat,text) in zip(block['parts'],rows)]
def g(key):return next(x for x in s['geo'] if x['key']==key)
replace(g('US'),[
(r'Consumer prices rise 2.7% annually in July|US Core CPI Picks Up','us_data',None,"The inflation argument is no longer a clean invitation to buy every rate-sensitive asset. The headline consumer measure offers relief, while the separate strength in core prices leaves room for a more cautious interpretation. The problem for equity owners is the distribution of the inflation burden: consumers can benefit from cheaper components of the basket even as businesses face pressure elsewhere. That makes pricing power more valuable than a generic growth label. Retain profitable franchises able to fund their own investment, and require evidence of margin protection before increasing exposure to businesses whose valuation already assumes easier policy. The release supports a debate about easing; it does not resolve the earnings consequences of tariffs."),
(r'US Fed to cut rates in September and once more this year|Goldman Sachs sees Fed cutting','us_macro',None,e['rates'].split('The portfolio question')[0]+"The poll is an expectation, whereas the Treasury curve is an observed financing price. Their agreement is incomplete: shorter maturities have eased over the longer comparison, but the long end still imposes a meaningful hurdle. Housing and indebted businesses need the cost of actual financing to improve, not just the probability of a policy change. Prefer an equity position supported by cash generation to one whose entire expected return comes from a lower discount rate."),
(r'Retail sales rise 0.5% in July|Consumer Sentiment Signals Caution After Solid US Retail Sales','us_data',None,q(r'US Producer Prices Rise by Most|Dollar up as US producer prices surge','us_data')+"The consumer is spending, yet the cost and confidence signals complicate the interpretation. AP's retail-sales description explicitly includes purchases brought forward ahead of tariffs; that raises the question of how much demand is being borrowed from a later period. Meanwhile stronger producer prices can squeeze the same businesses reporting respectable sales. Treat the combination as a margin-selection problem. Retail scale, inventory discipline and the ability to adjust assortment matter more than a broad declaration that consumption is either strong or weak. A business able to maintain profits through this mix deserves a different multiple from one defending sales by accepting lower returns."),
(r'Rate cut watch: All eyes on Fed Chair Powell|Fed Chair Jerome Powell may seriously disappoint','us_macro',None,"Keep the policy event conditional. An accommodating speech could extend the valuation trade without immediately changing households' purchasing decisions or companies' cost bases. A cautious message would be more uncomfortable for borrowers and expensive growth than for internally financed franchises. The allocation is therefore selective participation with liquid protection rather than a large binary wager on the tone of the speech. Add broader cyclical risk when the spending and margin evidence confirms that financing relief is reaching the real economy. Reduce duration-sensitive exposure if inflation concerns lift the long end even while investors continue to expect policy easing. The bond-market reaction will be the practical test of the message.")])
replace(g('EU'),[
(r'ECB|European Central Bank','europe',None,"For Europe, the attraction is a potentially more forgiving financing backdrop without paying the same growth premium attached to the most visible US technology businesses. The constraint is that exporters still face uncertain trade costs and customers. That argues for separating a domestic demand allocation from a recovery in global manufacturing. Banks, local services and industrial exporters can all respond to lower rates, but they need different confirmations. A lender needs creditworthy demand; an exporter needs repeat orders at a profitable price. Prefer the exposure that can demonstrate its improvement in cash earnings rather than buying the region as a single policy-sensitive block."),
(r'euro zone retail sales grow|German retail sales rise|eurozone.*inflation|euro zone.*inflation','europe','monthly',"Household activity offers a more useful cross-check than business sentiment alone. Stronger retail demand can support local services and distribution even while manufacturing remains uneven. But the volume and price components have to be distinguished: higher nominal sales do not automatically imply better real demand or stronger margins. The region's best equity opportunities may sit where consumers' purchasing power improves without a renewed input-cost shock. Watch whether lending and household confidence reinforce that improvement before widening the allocation into more heavily financed businesses. Currency translation can flatter reported overseas revenue, but it is a weaker substitute for customers buying more at an acceptable margin."),
(r'EU.*tariff|Europe.*tariff|European.*trade|German.*export','europe',None,"Trade predictability has value even when a negotiated framework leaves meaningful costs in place. The next corporate hurdle is whether management can price the product, manage production and commit to inventory with less fear of another abrupt change. Firms that already have local capacity or flexible sourcing have a different opportunity from those needing another large capital programme to adapt. Use relief in exporter shares to improve the quality of the holding rather than assuming that a policy compromise restores every pre-existing margin. The useful positive surprise would be customers placing profitable orders despite the new cost structure; the negative one would be management cutting investment because the commercial framework remains too uncertain."),
(r'European stocks|European shares|STOXX|Stoxx','europe',None,"Maintain a selective long bias where distributions, domestic activity or identifiable orders support the valuation. The case for increasing index exposure would strengthen if financial conditions and order books improve together. Until then, a narrow holding in a proven operator is more defensible than a broad wager on European industrial normalisation. Reduce the allocation if renewed trade friction meets a weaker consumer, because that would remove both the external and domestic support. For a foreign investor, decide explicitly whether to own the currency: a correct company view need not imply a conviction about the euro's next move.")])
replace(g('CN'),[
(r'China Stock Gauge Set for Decade High as Investors Dump Bonds|China.s Stock Rally Has The Makings','china',None,"China's most revealing development is the gap between equity optimism and the domestic demand evidence. A stronger stock market can reflect liquidity seeking a new home, confidence in strategic industries or a lower risk premium. None of those mechanisms requires a broad household recovery to have begun. That distinction makes a selective technology allocation easier to defend than a uniform cyclical call. Avoid treating the index as a referendum that has settled every argument about the economy. The next increase in exposure should be earned by cash flows, not by the elegance of the policy narrative. If investors are moving from bonds into equities, the share price can improve before the operating backdrop; the earnings hurdle then rises rather than disappears."),
(r'China.s July factory output, retail sales growth miss|China.s growth stumbles in July|China.s factory output, retail sales growth slump','china','monthly',"The July activity disappointment gives the rally a demanding fundamental test. Weakness in both production and household spending is harder to explain as an isolated industrial timing issue. For companies, the important distinction is whether sales can recover without a price concession that absorbs the benefit. A manufacturer serving a strategic technology programme may have better demand than a consumer supplier, but it still needs healthy cash collection. Prefer the company-level order book to a single national growth label. A durable improvement would show up across new demand, less pressure to discount and a more confident investment response. Until those signals align, the broad index can rise on liquidity while the more cyclical earnings outlook remains unsettled."),
(r'China July bank loans unexpectedly contract|China.s New Loans Plunge|China.s New Yuan Loans Drop','china',None,"The July lending weakness makes the policy response more urgent but also exposes its limitation. Credit cannot create a lasting demand impulse if households and private businesses remain reluctant to borrow. A subsidised funding offer helps the price of a loan; it does not automatically make a new investment attractive. That is why a bank-lending contraction deserves more attention than another broad promise of support. The investment implication is to seek borrowers with clear demand for their product and a credible return on incremental capital. Avoid assuming that every debt-sensitive asset benefits equally from easier policy. Confirmation would be a lending recovery linked to new spending and viable projects, rather than financing used primarily to manage existing liabilities."),
(r'China property easing unlikely to spark buying|China.s home prices slide|China.s new home prices fall again','china',None,"The latest skepticism about property easing reinforces the need for evidence from buyers rather than announcements. Removing a purchase restriction helps a household that already wants and can afford the property; it does less for a buyer worried about income, delivery or the value of existing housing wealth. A stabilising transaction market would matter more than a short-lived developer-share bounce because it would improve cash circulation through developers, suppliers and local finances. Keep property-sensitive materials and discretionary consumption separate from the technology allocation. The positive trigger is improving sales and cash collection without another deterioration in prices. Until that appears, the market can reward a policy option while the underlying property exposure remains a difficult balance-sheet trade."),
(r'China introduces loan interest subsidies|China offers interest subsidies|China pledges more financial support for consumption','china',None,"The consumption subsidy is an identifiable attempt to connect monetary support to household behaviour. It has a more direct transmission channel than an abstract promise of ample liquidity, but the response still depends on confidence and loan demand. Companies selling an eligible durable product may gain more immediately than a business waiting for a general recovery in consumer mood. Do not extrapolate that targeted channel into a forecast that every category of spending will accelerate. Trade arrangements and domestic support also solve different problems: predictable access can help an exporter plan, while households need confidence in their own income. The better portfolio combines exposure to demonstrated demand with the flexibility to broaden when the credit response becomes visible."),
(r'Alibaba, Baidu lead China.s fast-growing market for AI cloud services|China.*domestic.*chip|China.s Nvidia challenger Cambricon','china',None,"The fresh company-level picture is more interesting than a simple China reflation trade. Cloud demand and domestic chip development offer reasons for selected technology businesses to attract capital while property and household borrowing remain weak. But the value-chain distinctions matter: a cloud platform, an equipment supplier and a chip designer have different costs and customer dependencies. Choose the instrument that owns the economics being targeted. A mainland fund can express domestic industrial optimism while an offshore internet fund places more weight on platform monetisation and investor risk appetite. The allocation should therefore be deliberate about business model and listing exposure rather than using whichever China vehicle has just delivered the strongest price move."+obs('^HSI',(20,),'Hang Seng')+obs('000001.SS',(20,),'Shanghai Composite')+obs('ASHR',(20,),'ASHR')+obs('KWEB',(20,),'KWEB')+obs('CNY=X',(20,),'USD/CNY')),
(r'BHP.s Profit Slides to Five.Year Low as China Economy Drags|China.s Cement Slump','china',None,"The external earnings channel is a useful counterweight to the domestic technology excitement. Weakness tied to construction and bulk materials can coexist with spending on computing and strategic manufacturing. That is an argument for analysing the source of commodity demand rather than using a price as a universal growth thermometer. Copper's role in grids and computing infrastructure is an investable product story; household credit and housing activity are more direct evidence about the Chinese cycle. An exporter selling into construction needs a different risk allowance from a supplier serving a funded technology programme. The market becomes more attractive when improvement spreads beyond the favoured sectors, but the existing divergence should be respected rather than explained away."),
(r'China Stock Gauge Set for Decade High|China.s Stock Rally Has The Makings','china',None,"Keep selective exposure to technology franchises whose customer demand and funding can be demonstrated. Do not fund that position by assuming that property-linked cyclicals have already reached a durable turning point. Add broad domestic beta only when the lending and household activity evidence improves alongside the equity market; reduce it if the rally raises expectations while cash generation remains weak. Offshore and mainland exposure should be sized independently because their investors and earnings sensitivities differ. ⚠ Divergence: enthusiasm for domestic technology is advancing while July borrowing and activity describe a weaker private-demand backdrop. The opportunity is to own the profitable distinction, not to pretend that the rally has erased it.")])
replace(g('JP'),[
(r'Japan posts unexpectedly strong GDP|Japan.*GDP.*(?:growth|expan)','japan',None,"Japan's stronger activity report gives the normalisation debate an operating foundation beyond a currency move. Resilient exports can support aggregate growth even while households remain sensitive to prices, so the composition of the advance matters for equity selection. Exporters may benefit from orders yet remain exposed to a changing exchange rate; domestic financials need the improvement to reach lending and credit quality. Prefer businesses whose earnings can survive more than one currency outcome. The policy implication is a wider range of plausible paths rather than an automatic early move by the central bank. Watch whether wages and household demand validate the stronger headline before treating it as a complete domestic recovery."),
(r'Japan.*(?:wage|inflation|consumer)|yen.*(?:rise|fall|dollar)|Japanese.*export','japan',None,"The currency is the bridge between the growth result and the return available to a foreign investor. A stronger yen can improve imported purchasing power while challenging translated exporter earnings, which means the same macro change creates winners and losers. Domestic demand confirmation would make the equity thesis less dependent on translation. Keep hedged and unhedged exposures separate in the portfolio, rather than allowing a currency position to develop accidentally through an index fund. A broad market advance supported by lenders and household-facing businesses would be a more convincing signal of domestic improvement than a move confined to exporters."+obs('JPY=X',(20,),'USD/JPY')+obs('^N225',(20,),'Nikkei 225')),
(r'Bank of Japan|\bBOJ\b','japan',None,"Favour companies with a clear return on capital and retain exporters where the order case can withstand a less accommodating currency. Add domestic exposure if the stronger activity result is followed by improving household purchasing power, and reassess if higher costs arrive without matching income. The main risk to an unhedged foreign allocation is a rapid currency move overwhelming the company-level view. A gradual policy adjustment consistent with healthier demand would be easier for equities to absorb than an abrupt change prompted by imported price pressure. That difference should determine position size before the next policy headline appears.")])
replace(g('AU'),[
(r'Reserve Bank cuts cash rate to 3.6%|RBA.s third interest rate cut','australia',None,"Australia is now testing the transmission from the latest rate cut into household and business behaviour. The relief is concrete, but the distribution matters: a borrower whose lender passes it through quickly experiences a different cash-flow effect from one still waiting. That argues for monitoring actual repayments and profitable sales rather than buying the most leveraged consumer exposure on the day of a decision. Defensive income alternatives may also become more attractive as deposit returns change, yet a search for yield should not obscure balance-sheet risk. Prefer companies capable of benefiting from steadier demand without needing a rapid acceleration in housing prices or another immediate policy move."),
(r'Unemployment rate improvement tipped to keep RBA|Australia.*employment|Australian.*jobs','australia','monthly',"The labour-market constraint is important because improving employment can both support consumers and reduce the urgency of another cut. Equity investors should welcome healthy income even if it makes the next monetary step less predictable. A retailer relying on genuine purchasing power has a firmer foundation than one relying only on a lower discount rate. For lenders, household resilience helps asset quality while competition for deposits can still affect margins. Distinguish local demand exposure from resources whose customer base and product prices are driven elsewhere. A mixed macro backdrop rewards that separation rather than a uniform Australian cyclicals trade."+obs('AUDUSD=X',(20,),'AUD/USD')+obs('^AXJO',(20,),'ASX 200')),
(r'BHP.s Profit Slides|BlueScope boss warns|Soaring energy costs threaten','australia',None,"Keep resource exposure tied to actual product economics. The demand weakness affecting a bulk-material producer and the energy-cost pressure facing a manufacturer are different constraints, and domestic rate relief does not remove either one. Prefer businesses with enough funding flexibility to protect returns through a less favourable operating period. Increase household-sensitive risk if repayments and spending respond constructively to the cut; reduce it if the benefit is absorbed by saving or costs. For a foreign investor, the Australian dollar remains an additional risk decision, especially where commodity and domestic-demand exposures point in different directions.")])
replace(g('PL'),[
(r'Dynamika PKB Polski przyspieszyła|Potwierdziło się. Inflacja mocno w dół','poland_pl','monthly',"The Polish domestic story still has a constructive foundation in stronger activity and lower inflation. Bankier describes private consumption as the main driver of faster growth, while the inflation coverage gives households more room to retain purchasing power. The equity implication is selective exposure to spending and investment that can be earned in cash, rather than simply capitalising the possibility of additional rate cuts. A household-led improvement can support retailers and service businesses before a broader capital-expenditure cycle develops. For banks, however, the macro benefit now needs to be weighed against a more specific policy risk to profits. Keep the growth view positive while requiring a company-level bridge from the national result to shareholder earnings."),
(r'Takiej hossy na GPW|Pierwszy dywidendowy ETF w Polsce|Beta ETF Dywidenda Plus','poland_pl',None,"The introduction of a domestic dividend ETF adds a new distribution channel for income-oriented equity exposure. It does not by itself establish a measured inflow or guarantee that dividend shares will outperform. The useful question is whether companies can maintain payouts while funding their businesses through the next policy and investment cycle. Warsaw leadership also has to be read with the currency: international ownership can amplify the equity move, but a foreign investor receives a translated return. Keep banks, energy and consumer holdings separate enough that a sector-specific policy change does not silently dominate the whole allocation. An income label is helpful only when the underlying cash generation can sustain it."+obs('PLN=X',(20,),'USD/PLN')+obs('EURPLN=X',(20,),'EUR/PLN')+obs('EPOL',(20,),'EPOL')+obs('ETFBW20TR.WA',(20,),'WIG20TR ETF')+obs('PKO.WA',(20,),'PKO BP')+obs('PKN.WA',(20,),'Orlen')),
(r'Banki będą obłożone dodatkowym podatkiem|Deficyt budżetu państwa wyraźnie rośnie','poland_pl',None,"The proposed additional bank tax is the immediate challenge to an uncomplicated domestic-growth trade. Strong bank profits can make the sector politically attractive as a revenue source, while a wider fiscal deficit limits the government's room to leave that revenue uncollected. The investment question is how the burden would affect retained earnings, distributions and loan pricing. Do not assume that faster GDP growth translates proportionately into a shareholder benefit when the state is seeking a larger claim on sector profits. Terms and implementation remain crucial, so avoid assigning a precise earnings hit without an announced framework. Prefer a risk budget that can absorb an adverse policy change rather than treating the existing payout yield as fixed."),
(r'PKO BP bije rekord|Orlen chwali się odkryciem|Allegro największą pozycją','poland_pl',None,"The corporate picture offers more than a bank-tax story. PKO's reported strength, Orlen's gas discovery coverage and a major foreign fund's Allegro holding point to distinct routes into domestic investment, energy resources and platform economics. Each needs its own valuation framework. A discovery is not immediately distributable cash; a shareholder filing is not a permanent commitment; a record bank result can still face a new tax burden. Investors should map the catalyst to the economic claim actually owned. Companies with internally funded investment and visible cash conversion deserve preference over those whose upside depends entirely on another policy announcement. The benefit of a broad local recovery is that it creates alternatives when one sector's policy risk becomes less attractive."),
(r'Poland.*(?:Ukraine|NATO|defen)|Polska.*(?:Ukrain|NATO|obron)|polsk.*bezpieczeń|Ukrain','poland_pl',None,"Security remains both a spending theme and a financing consideration. Procurement creates an opportunity only for companies able to win and deliver profitable contracts, while regional uncertainty can raise the return investors require from the currency and sovereign debt. Avoid treating a diplomatic headline as a completed reduction in every risk premium. A more stable environment would improve the financing backdrop, but company execution still decides whether industrial demand benefits shareholders. Keep defence-adjacent positions sized to identifiable exposure rather than the scale of national spending ambitions. The portfolio can remain constructive on Polish domestic growth while retaining room to manage a less favourable regional development."),
(r'Banki będą obłożone dodatkowym podatkiem|Minister Domański zapowiada podatek bankowy','poland_pl',None,"The new decision point is whether the domestic recovery should be expressed through banks at the same weight as before. Strong operating profits are attractive, but they are also the basis for the proposed fiscal claim. A bank can remain a sound institution while becoming a less compelling equity at the existing valuation. Look for companies that benefit from improving demand without concentrating the same tax risk, and compare the price paid for those alternatives. The better policy outcome would preserve enough retained capital and profitability to support credit formation. The worse one would reduce the appeal of investment and distributions together. That range argues for selective exposure while the details remain unsettled."),
(r'Deficyt budżetu po lipcu|Deficyt budżetu państwa wyraźnie rośnie','poland_pl',None,"Retain exposure to a consumption-supported Polish recovery, but distribute it across businesses with distinct earnings drivers. Keep bank weights conditional on the eventual tax framework, and avoid counting expected distributions twice through both the earnings and valuation case. Add domestic cyclicals when profitable demand broadens; reduce them if fiscal or currency pressure absorbs the real-income benefit. The fiscal constraint also matters for long-duration projects whose financing assumptions are sensitive to sovereign yields. ⚠ Divergence: stronger activity and lower inflation support the operating economy, while the search for budget revenue can take a larger share of the same profits that attract equity investors. A sound macro view therefore needs a more selective sector expression.")])
