print('original Aug19 macro+sector rewrite saved')
replace(s['earnings_pattern'],[
(r'Nubank posts 42% profit boost','earnings','result',"Nubank's profit increase and reported share jump are a clean example of the market rewarding a delivered result. The lesson is not that every lender deserves a growth multiple, but that a specific franchise can produce an operating outcome strong enough to change expectations. Investors should ask what part is repeatable and how much further improvement the price now assumes. The result is more useful than a target increase because it describes a completed earnings period rather than a hoped-for next one."),
(r'CoreWeave shares drop as growing losses eclipse AI demand surge','earnings',None,"CoreWeave supplies the contrasting case: demand can be strong while the cost of serving it makes the equity less attractive. A revenue beat does not settle whether expansion earns enough after financing and investment. That distinction matters across the AI stack because an equipment vendor and a capacity owner can participate in the same customer programme with very different capital needs. A lower share price is an opportunity only if the shareholder economics remain defensible."),
(r'Palo Alto Networks reports earnings beat','earnings','result',"The fresh cybersecurity result broadens the operating comparison beyond the most capital-intensive AI names. A software franchise selling an important service can offer recurring demand without requiring the investor to finance a whole physical buildout. The founder's departure is an additional governance consideration, but it should not be allowed to replace the financial result as the basis for the earnings assessment. Compare the predictability of customer revenue, the required spending and the cash retained for shareholders before assigning the same technology premium to very different business models."),
(r'Nvidia.s AI Chip Demand Fuels Higher Earnings Projections|Morgan Stanley maintains bullish stance on Nvidia','earnings',None,"The Nvidia coverage belongs in the preview column. Analyst projections can help identify a potential positive surprise, but they also raise the price of meeting expectations. The market can reward actual profitability in one company while paying in advance for a result in another. That creates an event-risk asymmetry: confidence needs to be supported by delivered revenue, margins and a credible outlook. Do not cite a prediction of an earnings beat as if the company has already produced it."),
(r'How retail accounting could distort profitability as tariffs take effect','earnings',None,"For the next retail results, add inventory timing to the usual demand and margin checklist. A business may sell goods purchased under one cost framework while replacing them under another, so the current gross-profit figure may be a poor guide to the next period. Hold demonstrated earnings quality and keep preview-driven positions smaller. Increase exposure when the result explains the bridge from sales to recurring cash; reduce it when the headline looks strong but the replacement-cost or investment burden weakens the economics.")])
s['earnings_pattern']['title']='Delivered cash economics beat a borrowed industry narrative'
s['underowned']=[{'title':title,'parts':[[label,q(rx,topic)+text] for label,rx,topic,text in rows]} for title,rows in [
('Polish demand beyond the bank-tax target',[
('Attention Gap',r'Banki będą obłożone dodatkowym podatkiem','poland_pl',"The new tax debate can obscure the constructive consumption backdrop. This is an analytical distinction, not a claim about measured institutional underweights. A domestic recovery can create earnings outside the sector being asked to contribute more fiscal revenue."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Dynamika PKB Polski przyspieszyła','poland_pl',"Selected consumer and service franchises offer an alternative expression of household demand. Their risk is competitive pricing or weaker spending, rather than the identical tax exposure carried by a bank. Valuation still has to compensate for that operating risk."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'Banki będą obłożone dodatkowym podatkiem|Minister Domański zapowiada podatek bankowy','poland_pl',"Compare the eventual tax terms with bank distributions and lending incentives. Increase nonbank domestic exposure if profitable demand holds up while the relative banking claim becomes less attractive. Reverse that preference if the policy burden proves modest and bank valuations already compensate for it.")]),
('China cloud demand versus the construction drag',[
('Attention Gap',r'Alibaba, Baidu lead China.s fast-growing market for AI cloud services','china',"Cloud demand offers a more specific growth channel than a general call on Chinese reflation. The attraction is a customer business that can develop while household borrowing and housing remain weak. That divergence deserves deliberate exposure rather than a broad index assumption."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'China.s Nvidia challenger Cambricon|China.*domestic.*chip','china',"A cloud platform and a chip developer do not earn the same return. Prefer a listed vehicle with a clear claim on the demand being targeted; recognise the capital and competitive risk in domestic substitution."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'China.s July factory output, retail sales growth miss|China July bank loans unexpectedly contract','china',"The position broadens only if demand improvement spreads beyond strategic technology. Until then, keep the property-sensitive cyclical hedge separate. Stronger customer monetisation would validate the technology exposure; an advance driven only by a higher valuation would warrant trimming it.")]),
('Who owns the nuclear customer’s cash flow?',[
('Attention Gap',r'Google, Kairos Power plan advanced nuclear plant','retail',"The named power customer attracts attention, but the investable chain is less obvious. An announced project supports interest in the industry without proving that each listed developer or fuel supplier has won an order."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Morgan Stanley says nuclear power is gaining momentum','retail',"Listed uranium, generation and development exposures offer different payoffs. Use the security that owns the intended economics and avoid describing an indirect thematic holding as a contract beneficiary. Funding and execution remain central."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'Google, Kairos Power plan advanced nuclear plant','retail',"Look for contracts, licensing progress and financing that place the development risk with parties able to bear it. Add only as those commitments become credible. A longer timetable or weaker return allocation would undermine the equity case even if eventual electricity demand remains attractive.")]),
('Cybersecurity cash alongside AI capital spending',[
('Attention Gap',r'Palo Alto Networks reports earnings beat','earnings',"The fresh operating result offers a contrast with the attention attached to building physical AI capacity. A recurring service can justify investment through established customer economics rather than a promise that an expensive asset base will eventually be fully utilised."),
('Exposure & Risk',r'Palo Alto Networks reports earnings beat','earnings',"Palo Alto provides a specific equity expression, while a diversified software holding reduces company risk at the cost of diluting this particular catalyst. The management transition and valuation remain important even after a beat."),
('Trigger to Watch',r'CoreWeave shares drop as growing losses eclipse AI demand surge','earnings',"Compare retained cash and the capital required for each additional customer across the two models. Increase the recurring-service preference when operating evidence supports it; reverse it if infrastructure returns improve enough to compensate for the financing burden.")])]]
replace(s['crypto'],[
(r'Bitcoin, ethereum slip as crypto markets pull back|Bitcoin Price, XRP, Ethereum Fall','crypto',None,"The pullback changes the immediate question from how large the next audience might become to whether existing buyers remain willing to hold risk. Price weakness does not erase improvements in access, but it tests positions built on an uninterrupted rise. Distinguish the direct token from an equity wrapper whose market can close while the asset continues trading. A shareholder in a treasury business carries financing and dilution risk in addition to the token view. That combination can amplify a reversal even when the long-term asset narrative remains plausible."+obs('BTC-USD',(1,20),'Bitcoin')+obs('ETH-USD',(1,20),'Ether')+obs('SOL-USD',(1,20),'Solana')),
(r'SEC Punts on Trump Media Bitcoin and Ethereum ETF Decision|SEC delays XRP, Dogecoin','crypto',None,"The regulatory timetable remains a risk rather than a guaranteed demand event. A delayed decision can preserve eventual optionality while withholding the near-term catalyst investors wanted. Do not treat a pending product as an approved channel for new capital. The wider market also has to distinguish a change in access from a change in economic use: both may matter, but they are separate reasons to own the asset. A more resilient demand base would show itself through orderly financing and price behaviour during weakness, rather than through the confidence of another ambitious price forecast."),
(r'Ethereum treasury firm SharpLink stock dips|BitMine files to expand.*offering','crypto',None,"Prefer a direct token holding when the investment thesis is token demand. A treasury equity needs an additional answer about the terms on which it buys assets and the share of those assets belonging to each existing investor. Maintain room to reduce risk if liquidity deteriorates or the equity premium contracts. A larger aggregate token balance can coexist with an unattractive shareholder outcome when funding is expensive. The useful positive trigger is improved per-share economics supported by real demand; the negative one is a financing loop that needs ever more optimistic prices simply to keep working.")])
s['crypto']['title']='The pullback tests access, liquidity and the equity-wrapper premium'
replace(s['flows'],[
(r'Goldman Sachs sees Fed cutting 3 times|US Fed to cut rates in September and once more','us_macro',None,"The policy forecast and the liquidity outcome should remain separate in the risk budget. An economist's expectation of cuts can support an asset-price rally before any financing terms actually change. Companies with debt to refinance need the latter, while an internally funded franchise can tolerate a more uncertain timetable. That difference favours balance-sheet quality when the market is paying for relief in advance. The constructive scenario is easing that reaches viable borrowers while spending remains resilient. The dangerous version is a valuation expansion that leaves little room for the central bank to disappoint. Avoid building several ostensibly different positions around that one policy outcome."),
(r'Fed.s Goolsbee sees.*unease|US Producer Prices Rise by Most','us_macro',None,"Inflation unease matters because the long end can resist the relief priced into shorter maturities. A dovish policy path is less useful to housing and capital-intensive investment if long-term funding remains demanding. The dollar introduces another transmission channel: a softer currency may ease global financing but can also alter imported costs and foreign investors' translated returns. Keep the currency and duration exposures visible rather than allowing them to accumulate through equity holdings. The observed prices are a better guide to the financing burden than a broad claim that policy has become supportive."+obs('DX-Y.NYB',(20,),'DXY')+obs('TLT',(20,),'TLT')),
(r'CoreWeave.*(?:loss|debt|financing)|Galaxy closes.*debt facility','flows',None,"The infrastructure buildout provides a practical credit test. A funded project can proceed even while the equity investor debates whether the return compensates for the capital required. Debt capacity is helpful, but the assets still need customers and a margin sufficient to service the financing. Distinguish investment-grade operating resilience from speculative access to another round of funding. Broad bond funds offer context, not proof that every issuer has the same terms. A market that rewards recurring cash generation while challenging capital-intensive expansion would be discriminating rather than uniformly closed to risk."+obs('HYG',(20,),'HYG')+obs('LQD',(20,),'LQD')),
(r'China Stock Gauge Set for Decade High as Investors Dump Bonds','china',None,"The reported move from Chinese bonds toward equities illustrates how capital can change destination before the operating cycle turns. It can support a stock rally without proving that household credit has recovered. Meanwhile the Polish dividend ETF introduces a potential distribution channel, but its existence alone does not establish the amount of fresh buying. These distinctions matter when interpreting flows: a change in instrument access, a reallocation among existing assets and new savings entering the market have different implications. Avoid assigning a permanent marginal buyer to an asset on the strength of a single announcement. Require persistence and earnings support before increasing a crowded directional exposure."),
(r'BofA.s Hartnett Sees Profit.Taking in Stocks After Jackson Hole|Fed Chair Jerome Powell may seriously disappoint','us_macro',None,"The portfolio implication is to retain participation while reducing dependence on a perfect policy message. Hold enough liquid exposure to respond if financing conditions improve constructively, but do not borrow heavily against a speech that has yet to occur. Pair cyclical holdings with franchises whose returns depend on identifiable customers and internal funding. Keep commodity and foreign-currency allocations tied to their own mechanisms. If bonds, credit and earnings begin to contradict the equity narrative, reduce the least self-financing exposures first. If they align, broaden through companies whose valuations have not already absorbed the entire prospective benefit.")])
s['flows']['title']='Expected easing, actual financing and the destination of capital'
